  "id": "schematic-representation",
  "term": "schematic representation",
  "definition": "Schematic representation is a simplified depiction that keeps the most relevant features of a scene, such as important structural edges and object outlines, while leaving out much of the original visual detail. In this context, it is used to make limited visual input easier to interpret for recognizing objects and understanding indoor environments.",
